01:20:37,140 --> 01:20:37,500
Yes.

1171
01:20:37,700 --> 01:20:38,460
He's the Republican.

1172
01:20:38,680 --> 01:20:38,860
My rival.

1173
01:20:39,040 --> 01:20:39,200
Yes.

1174
01:20:39,500 --> 01:20:40,200
My Samaritan.

1175
01:20:40,620 --> 01:20:42,020
He's the candidate you're running against.

1176
01:20:42,180 --> 01:20:42,440
Yes.

1177
01:20:42,860 --> 01:20:46,300
Um, you've said that Ken is one of the most corrupt politicians in America.

1178
01:20:47,200 --> 01:20:47,600
Yes.

1179
01:20:47,740 --> 01:20:48,180
Do you love him?

1180
01:20:48,620 --> 01:20:48,880
Yes.

1181
01:20:49,920 --> 01:20:51,340
Ken Paxton is a child of God.

1182
01:20:52,040 --> 01:20:53,780
He is my brother in Christ.

1183
01:20:54,560 --> 01:20:56,680
It doesn't mean there's not accountability, right?

1184
01:20:56,760 --> 01:20:57,920
Love requires accountability.

1185
01:20:57,920 --> 01:21:02,820
Um, we talked about the story of my mom and her love meant standing up to a bully.

1186
01:21:03,420 --> 01:21:06,780
And, you know, if you think about when you're like.

1187
01:21:06,780 --> 01:21:20,860
Out having a drink with your friends and your friend grabs their car keys to drive home under the influence, your job as their friend is to take those keys away, to physically block them from getting in the car.

1188
01:21:21,660 --> 01:21:24,400
And that feels, um, aggressive.

1189
01:21:24,920 --> 01:21:36,760
It feels maybe even hostile, but it is done out of love for that person and for everybody else, for all of your neighbors, Ken Paxton from every, I don't know, Ken Paxton personally.

